==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|κιρρός||tawny}} and {{m|en|-osis}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/sɪˈɹoʊsɪs/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|cirrhoses}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} A chronic disease of the [[liver]] caused by damage from [[toxin]]s (including [[alcohol]]), metabolic problems, [[hepatitis]] or nutritional deprivation. It is characterised by an increase of fibrous tissue and the destruction of liver cells.
# {{lb|en|by extension}} Interstitial inflammation of kidneys, lungs, and other organs.

